    <briefdescription>
<para>Render-ready shader bundle — built at load time, used at render time. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><ref refid="structshader_1_1_pass" kindref="compound">Pass</ref> is the shader pipeline&apos;s equivalent of Segments in the LAF graphics pipeline: where Segments is a paint-ready SVG bundle produced by getSegments(), <ref refid="structshader_1_1_pass" kindref="compound">Pass</ref> is a render-ready shader bundle produced by <ref refid="structshader_1_1_compiler_1adee5f8ed1b195826f783d1224c8077f7" kindref="member">Compiler::buildPass()</ref>. Both are dumb data — no machinery state.</para>
<para>program owns the linked shader. setUniforms is a baked dispatch function: all active <ref refid="juce__gl_8h_1a5ac0f3c4d7fafd42b284b5487a791017" kindref="member" external="/Users/jreng/Documents/Poems/JUCE/docs/tagfile.xml">GLint</ref> locations are captured by value in the lambda closure at build time (<ref refid="structshader_1_1_compiler_1adee5f8ed1b195826f783d1224c8077f7" kindref="member">Compiler::buildPass</ref>). Inactive uniforms (location -1) are GL no-ops — the if-checks inside setUniforms are baked at build time, not per-frame null guards. No <ref refid="structjuce_1_1OpenGLShaderProgram_1_1Uniform" kindref="compound" external="/Users/jreng/Documents/Poems/JUCE/docs/tagfile.xml">juce::OpenGLShaderProgram::Uniform</ref> objects are used — those assert on inactive uniforms.</para>
<para>fbos is std::nullopt for the screen pass (ID::image) and a <ref refid="structshader_1_1_swap_chain" kindref="compound">SwapChain</ref> for buffer passes (ID::bufferA..D). <ref refid="structshader_1_1_swap_chain" kindref="compound">SwapChain</ref> owns and releases its FBOs.</para>
<para>Thread contract: GL THREAD only. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
